{"changes":["eka-core/codegraph/codegraph.go: `Index.StatKey` records a fingerprint of the inventoried set from path, size and mtime (`UnixNano`, so the representation cannot vary by locale or carry a monotonic component). Additive with omitempty; `Digest` is untouched because it is the identity used elsewhere.","eka-core/codegraph/codegraph.go: `walkDir` became `walkEntries`, taking a per-file callback. The build and the new `currentStatKey` both go through it, so the set of files a build indexes and the set a fingerprint covers cannot drift: a hit granted for a tree that would build differently is a correctness bug, worse than a slow cache. The old shape could not have this guarantee because a second walker would have been free to disagree about skip rules or symlinked directories.","eka-core/codegraph/codegraph.go: `LoadOrBuildWithOptions` no longer builds to check freshness. A cache is a hit when its StatKey matches one directory walk; a cache without StatKey is never a hit, so old caches stay correct and are rewritten with the fingerprint on first read. A miss builds exactly once, where the old code could build twice.","eka-core/codegraph/codegraph.go: the build now accumulates the fingerprint inside its own traversal rather than walking again, so a miss costs one walk, not two."],"role":"implementation","summary":"Made the code-graph cache trustworthy from filesystem metadata, so a hit parses nothing.","tests":["eka-core codegraph/cache_test.go (4 tests): a hit performs no build work (parseCount unchanged across the second call); a same-size different-mtime change and a size change both miss; a cache JSON without StatKey is rebuilt and then upgraded so the next call hits; touching files under .git, node_modules or exchange does not move the fingerprint; with FollowSymlinks=false a symlinked directory never appears in the fingerprint while touching an indexed file still moves it.","Non-vacuous proof: with only the old algorithm restored, TestCacheHitParsesNothing reports \"cache hit parsed: parseCount 3 -\u003e 6\" — six file reads for a two-file tree, because the build ran twice. With the change the same call parses nothing.","go test ./codegraph/... -count=1 -\u003e ok. go test ./... -count=1 in eka-core -\u003e all 13 packages ok. go build ./... , go vet ./... , gofmt -l . -\u003e clean."]}